  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Collection",
      "items": [
        "The collector orchestrator runs ten registered collectors and records successes, failures, and newly discovered item count.",
        "Jane Street uses JSON discovery, an OCaml text filter, and position-page parsing before storage."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Scoring and ranking",
      "items": [
        "The OCaml executable deterministically detects domain signals and totals their weights; the current workflow builds it but does not run the deterministic-score command.",
        "Candidate eligibility and the final 70% technical + 30% practical score are implemented in OCaml. Python adapters exchange validated JSON with the compiled executable, while Python retains database operations and orchestration."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Automation and delivery",
      "items": [
        "The workflow restores and later pushes the database through a private state repository.",
        "Telegram credentials and the workflow's LLM key are supplied as GitHub Actions secrets."
      ]
    }
  ]
